{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dyXyp24uPS8JXUUb6PG5H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Number audit: shared instructions for every auditor (loop0008 item 07, 2026-10-03)\n2\t\n3\tYou audit EVERY quantitative claim in your assigned document(s) in /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/.\n4\tA quantitative claim = any number stated as a fact (counts, percentages, times, node counts,\n5\tcore-hours, page/section/theorem numbers of citations, sizes, dates of measurement, Lean theorem\n6\tnames cited as the source of a fact, \"all N\", \"k of N\"). Skip pure numbering of our own sections\n7\tand pure arithmetic examples inside proofs unless they state a result (e.g. \"close = 3\" in a\n8\tcounterexample IS a claim: check it against the Lean theorem or a script).\n9\t\n10\tFor each claim, record ONE table row:\n11\t| line | claim (short, with the value) | source (regenerate command / CSV / JSON / Lean theorem / held PDF+page) | check done | status |\n12\t\n13\tStatus is one of:\n14\t- REPRODUCED: you re-ran the command or recomputed from raw data now and got the same value.\n15\t- MATCHES-RECORD: matches the recorded data file / tables.md / log / Lean theorem statement (grep), not rerun.\n16\t- DRIFT: does not match; give the correct value and the evidence.\n17\t- STALE: was true when written but superseded by later events (e.g. a run that has since finished).\n18\t- UNSOURCED: no source found in the repository; say what you searched.\n19\t- UNCHECKED: checkable only by a run beyond the budget; say why.\n20\t\n21\tGroup repeated mentions of the same number in a row (\"lines 12, 340, 902\").\n22\t\n23\tRULES\n24\t- Compute budget: at most ONE core for you, and no single command longer than ~10 minutes.\n25\t  Prefix any Python run with `nice -n 10`. The machine is shared with a 20-core run\n26\t  (`paper2.solver_fix_split`, PID in paper2/data/solver_fix_split.pid): never stop, restart or\n27\t  edit it, `paper2/solver_fix_split.py`, or `paper2/data/solver_fix_split_*`. Do NOT run\n28\t  `python -m paper2.solver_fix_split --tables` (it writes a file); `--summary` is read-only and fine.\n29\t- Never write to solutions/. Never run benchmarks.csearch / recertify / overnight. Never commit.\n30\t  Never edit CLAUDE.md. Never edit any .lean file. Do not run `lake build` (the gate does that);\n31\t  for Lean, grep the theorem name and read its statement.\n32\t- Prefer checking against recorded data (CSVs, *_tables.md, JSON, logs). Rerun a script only if\n33\t  it is cheap (read its docstring/argparse first; make sure it does not overwrite recorded data\n34\t  files with different parameters — if it writes, either use a --out option to a scratch path\n35\t  under /tmp, or do not run it). Python is `python3`; run from /home/al/dev/MOSP with `-m`.\n36\t- Literature citations: check page/section numbers against the held PDF in literature/\n37\t  (`pdftotext -layout file.pdf - | grep -n ...`). Do not fetch from the web.\n38\t- FIX every DRIFT in the source document you were assigned (only those documents), with the\n39\t  Edit tool, minimal change, keeping the author's style (short plain sentences). For a STALE\n40\t  claim, add a short dated note \"*(2026-10-03, number audit: ...)*\" rather than rewriting history,\n41\t  unless the text is a present-tense status line, in which case update it and say so.\n42\t  Do not touch other documents; if a drift is in another document, report it instead.\n43\t- Output: write your full report to /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/data/number_audit/<NAME>.md with\n44\t  (1) a header: document(s), line count, number of claims, counts per status;\n45\t  (2) the table;\n46\t  (3) \"Fixes made\": file:line, old -> new, evidence;\n47\t  (4) \"Drifts in other documents\" if any.\n48\t  Your final reply to me: the status counts, the list of fixes, and anything alarming\n49\t  (especially any sign a certified value or a theorem claim is wrong). Keep the reply under 400 words.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYmNAjY4LckXdAkhBVmMxy","session_id":"8829a219-b7d6-4bcd-a71b-6b4a7da5f863","uuid":"50e83cf7-2fcc-4d3f-8015-40a2e3179030","timestamp":"2026-10-03T06:03:40.040Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit equivalences.md numbers"}
