ee that MTSP is NP-hard\n   and even if that is true, we cannot guarantee that\n   MOSP is NP-hard. In fact, MOSP is equivalent to\n   MTSP only when C = C *\n      We make the observation that if C > C*, an\n   optimal solution to MTSP may not be an optimal\n   solution to the MOSP. The converse, however, is\n   always true.\n      When C < C * , an optimal solution to the MTSP\n   may not be an optimal solution to the MOSP and\n   vice-versa.\nerational Research 100 (1997) 454-463","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYmNAjY4LckXdAkhBVmMxy","session_id":"8829a219-b7d6-4bcd-a71b-6b4a7da5f863","uuid":"d01048be-016d-49e4-9604-f2a2987d3c4a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T06:06:14.837Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit equivalences.md numbers"}
