{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRZa2wRZucTC5aiqMV9WYZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Linhares and Yanasse - 2002 - Connections between cutting-pattern sequencing, VL.pdf\nchu_2011_phd_thesis_improving_combinatorial_optimization.pdf\nfink_2012_phd_thesis_mosp_novas_contribuicoes.pdf\nohtsuki_mori_kuh_kashiwabara_fujisawa_1979_one_dimensional_logic.pdf\npoliquit_2008_thesis_mosp_method.pdf\nugrep: warning: literature/MANIFEST.md: No such file or directory\n# Independent brute force: does the thesis's Theorem 6.3.8 (better move, premise\n# close(q,S) >= open(q, S+r)) fail on cexGraph at k = 6?  And Theorem 6.3.6?\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nM = [2201,102,30,13,21,6690,8514,9857,3904,4000,16256,3873,13344,13504]\nn, K = 14, 6\nassert all(M[i] >> i & 1 for i in range(n))\nassert all((M[i] >> j & 1) == (M[j] >> i & 1) for i in range(n) for j in range(n))\nFULL = (1 << n) - 1\ndef N(S):\n    r = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if S >> i & 1: r |= M[i]\n    return r\npc = lambda x: bin(x).count(\"1\")\ndef cost(S, q):          # stacks open while q's stack closes after S\n    return pc((N(S) | M[q]) & ~S)\n@lru_cache(None)\ndef sol(S):\n    if S == FULL: return True\n    return any(not S >> q & 1 and cost(S, q) <= K and sol(S | 1 << q) for q in range(n))","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V8DKfNe5gXB4gDSFXTX7zp","session_id":"8829a219-b7d6-4bcd-a71b-6b4a7da5f863","uuid":"7abcb80f-4728-407d-a10d-08a07e6d3670","timestamp":"2026-10-03T06:07:23.473Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit popularity.md and plan.md"}
