{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nZWGntA9rP36TqizuDksZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1128\t  default in both. Section 4.4.4 lists the checks.\n1129\t- **Re-certification: 108 of 115 done, 7 left.** Values certified by the\n1130\t  subset-lattice oracle, by a checked DRAT refutation through the SAT path, by\n1131\t  the SAT binary search before the customer search existed, or by a lower bound\n1132\t  equal to the value, do not depend on the search and stand as they are (6,259\n1133\t  of the 6,374 certified values). The other 115 rested on the customer search\n1134\t  under the published rules. The repaired solver re-refutes $\\text{value} - 1$\n1135\t  on 108 of them (106 of 113 distinct graphs; every one at 40–100 customers and\n1136\t  16 of 23 at 125 × 125), in $9.73 \\times 10^{10}$ nodes. **No value changed.**\n1137\t  The 7 left are 125 × 125 instances at densities 2 and 4\n1138\t  (`Random-125-125-2-{1,4,5}_0`, `Random-125-125-4-{1,2,4,5}_0`), censored\n1139\t  after 10.1 hours each at $5.0$–$6.9 \\times 10^{10}$ nodes and priced at 13 to\n1140\t  153 core-hours each, which is probably low. They keep their values as\n1141\t  verified upper bounds. For them the refutation of $\\text{value} - 1$ under\n1142\t  the repaired rules is still to be made, and none of the old runs passes the\n1143\t  audit of section 4.4.4. A resumable runner continues them\n1144\t  (`solver_fix.md`, item 07, \"Needs a long run\").\n1145\t- **The certificate route: left.** The certificate checker's definite and\n1146\t  better steps must check the repaired premises, and the emitter must model the\n1147\t  repaired rules: one matching per step. With that change, an accepted\n1148\t  certificate proves $Z(M) > k$ by Theorem 4.19's chain without trusting the\n1149\t  search, which is the route this paper's dataset relies on for values the SAT\n1150\t  path cannot reach. Item 07's walk is a first form of the check, run outside\n1151\t  the checker.\n1152\t  *Done 2026-10-03 (loop0008 item 05, `certificates.md`).* The emitter models\n1153\t  the repaired rules, and each definite and better step carries its matching.\n1154\t  An independent checker, `certificate_check.py`, verifies the matchings. On\n1155\t  the corpus at 9–75 customers, 6,276 refutations verify and none is\n1156\t  rejected; 10 instances at 75 customers did not emit within 60 s. The\n1157\t  published rules' certificate on `DEFINITE_CEX` from {2} is rejected.\n1158\t- **A faster route for the 7, proposed and not built.** The repaired filter is\n1159\t  node-sound at the root, and by Theorem 4.18 each root child can be refuted in\n1160\t  its own process from its own state with no old moves and an empty memo. That\n1161\t  spreads one refutation over many cores. It needs a C entry point that starts\n1162\t  from a given state, and a short Lean statement of the composition.\n1163\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BsdCMDhc13EqCvGf8RgjDc","session_id":"8829a219-b7d6-4bcd-a71b-6b4a7da5f863","uuid":"d016f54b-6832-4cf4-ae0b-046140b48ce2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T06:08:58.441Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit revised_algorithm.md numbers"}
